# The packaging set (#952).
#
# `micold-packaging` marks paths that can change the shipped packages or how they are built. No
# ci.yml job is gated on it since the Windows ARM64 package job went with #1897. A path is outside
# the set until declared; the
# failure direction is "run it". Read by scripts/classify-change.sh (`packaging=` output), pinned by
# scripts/tests/classify-change.test.sh. Later gates add their own attribute the same way.
packaging/**                          micold-packaging
/Cargo.toml                           micold-packaging
/Cargo.lock                           micold-packaging
/.github/workflows/release.yml        micold-packaging
# Inputs the package builds read beside the set above: the licences, the scripts they call, and
# the toolchain pins.
/LICENSE                              micold-packaging
/assets/fonts/LICENSE*                micold-packaging
/assets/fonts/PROVENANCE.md           micold-packaging
scripts/remote-daemon-bundle.sh       micold-packaging
scripts/build-lock.sh                 micold-packaging
/rust-toolchain.toml                  micold-packaging
/.cargo/config.toml                   micold-packaging

# The daemon-runtime set (#954).
#
# `micold-daemon-runtime` marks paths that can change what the real-runtime jobs of ci.yml build
# or test: `sandbox against a real runtime` (the `sandbox_real_*` targets of micold-core and
# micold-daemon, against the :dev sandbox and basic images), and `remote daemon over a real sshd`
# (the `ssh_real_*` targets of micold-daemon). One attribute serves all three: their code paths are
# the same crates, the sandbox jobs only add the image directories, and the sshd job (about five
# minutes) is never the critical path, so a second attribute would buy a minute-scale saving at
# the price of a second output to keep in step. Pull requests run the jobs only when a change
# touches the set -- or carries `full-ci` -- and main pushes and the nightly always run them. A path
# is outside the set until declared; the failure direction is "run it". Read by scripts/classify-change.sh (`daemon_runtime=` output), pinned by
# scripts/tests/classify-change.test.sh.
crates/micold-core/**                 micold-daemon-runtime
crates/micold-daemon/**               micold-daemon-runtime
/Cargo.toml                           micold-daemon-runtime
/Cargo.lock                           micold-daemon-runtime
/rust-toolchain.toml                  micold-daemon-runtime
/.cargo/config.toml                   micold-daemon-runtime
# The two images the sandbox job builds, and the script that pins the basic image's content hash.
packaging/sandbox/**                  micold-daemon-runtime
packaging/basic/**                    micold-daemon-runtime
scripts/basic-image-hash.sh           micold-daemon-runtime
# The workflow itself: an edit to a job's steps is proven by the PR that makes it.
/.github/workflows/ci.yml             micold-daemon-runtime

